Reject DMA-BUF export when neither Vulkan SYNC_FD nor implicit synchronization
is available. Memory-FD support alone does not make the exported image safe
for another API. In particular PanVK kbase advertises external memory but
cannot create SYNC_FD semaphores. Zink later dereferences an empty signal
semaphore array in submit_queue when such a resource is used again.

Refuse before add_resource_bind can convert the texture into an exportable
resource. EGL export then fails and applications such as Ghostty 1.4 use GPU
rendering with CPU readback presentation. Drivers with native fence support
or implicit synchronization keep their existing export path.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
@@ -2210,6 +2210,13 @@ zink_resource_get_handle(struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
                          struct winsys_handle *whandle,
                          unsigned usage)
 {
+   struct zink_screen *zs = zink_screen(pscreen);
+   /* External memory support alone does not provide producer/consumer sync.
+    * Reject before add_resource_bind makes this texture exportable.
+    */
+   if (whandle->type == WINSYS_HANDLE_TYPE_FD &&
+       !pscreen->caps.native_fence_fd && !zs->driver_workarounds.implicit_sync)
+      return false;
    if (tex->target == PIPE_BUFFER)
       tc_buffer_disable_cpu_storage(tex);
 #ifdef HAVE_LIBDRM
